=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTATION_DEFINITION_CHANGED
title: Editing an expectation inside a pytest.param row
bypass: 86a
note: F-067 (research E-11). `_param_columns` reads a `pytest.param(...)`
note2: row as one cell, so every cell after the first never reached the
note3: column text. Wrapping a row for an id alone (no marks, no other
note4: change) took its expectation out of the only text this rule
note5: compared, and the edit was free. The row structure keeps every cell.
note6: 100.0 is what a tax-ignoring invoice_total returns for the pair; the
note7: other row is one that bug cannot fail.
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        pytest.param([50.0, 50.0], 105.0, id="pair"),
        ([], 0.0),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        pytest.param([50.0, 50.0], 100.0, id="pair"),
        ([], 0.0),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
